<title>USA: Video Update to acquire Canadian chain.</title>
<headline>Video Update to acquire Canadian chain.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Video Update Inc said Tuesday it has signed a letter of intent to acquire the assets of Superior Video, a 27-store video rental chain based in British Columbia, from  Hill-Cassidy Retail Corp.</p>
<p>Financial terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Final closing of the acquisition is subject to Canadian regulatory approval, Video Update board and lender approval, due diligence and signing of a definitive agreement, the company said.</p>
<p>Shares of Video Update, a video retail chain with 333 video superstores in North America, were down 2/16 at 4-13/16 Tuesday.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
